  "id": "COMPOUND:9128 - PROTEIN:367",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Ensulizole may interact with S-methylmethionine--homocysteine S-methyltransferase BHMT2 through a series of target relationships. Ensulizole is directly linked to Serine--tRNA ligase, cytoplasmic, which in turn is targeted by certolizumab pegol and by 13-[(2R,3R,4R)-3,4-dihydroxy-2-(hydroxymethyl)-3,4-dihydro-2H-pyrrol-5-yl]-1-hydroxytridecan-5-one. Both of these compounds are also targets of BHMT2, indicating a potential pathway through which Ensulizole may influence BHMT2 activity. The shared involvement of Serine--tRNA ligase, cytoplasmic in multiple pathways suggests a possible mechanism of action involving the regulation of methylation processes, which are critical for various cellular functions. The consistent scores across the three paths further support the notion of a direct or indirect relationship between Ensulizole and BHMT2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
